<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired"><h2>What it inspired</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Aristocracy Forever (Little Red Songbook)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">satire</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Women's verses</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1970s</span><span class="sg-chain-h">added verses</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Pete Seeger's adaptation</span><span class="sg-chain-h">rewritten last verse, two verses dropped</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Verses by Steve Suffet (Little Red Songbook, centennial edition)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">added verses</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Pride (film)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2014</span><span class="sg-chain-h">sung in</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">The Battle Hymn of Cooperation</span><span class="sg-chain-h">possibly inspired, same tune</span></li></ul></section>
<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired-by"><h2>What it drew on</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><a href="/songs/john-browns-body">John Brown's Body</a> <span class="sg-chain-y">1861</span><span class="sg-chain-h">same tune</span></li><li><a href="/songs/battle-hymn-of-the-republic">Battle Hymn of the Republic</a> <span class="sg-chain-y">1862</span><span class="sg-chain-h">same tune</span></li></ul></section>
